package cajeta.net.http;

import cajeta.lang.String;

/**
 * Thrown by the [`HttpServer`](HttpServer.cajeta) request path (plan item
 * **NET-9.6**) when an inbound request **body exceeds the configured size
 * cap** ([`ServerLimits.maxBodyBytes`](ServerLimits.cajeta)). The body-side
 * counterpart of [`HeadersTooLargeException`](HeadersTooLargeException.cajeta)
 * (which guards the *head*): a declared `Content-Length` over the ceiling is
 * rejected **up front** — before any body byte is buffered — and a
 * `Transfer-Encoding: chunked` body that *streams* past the ceiling is
 * rejected the moment its decoded total crosses it, so a hostile upload can
 * never force unbounded buffering.
 *
 * The `limit` field carries the configured byte ceiling that was crossed,
 * and `observed` the body size reached (the declared `Content-Length`, or
 * the decoded-so-far total for a chunked stream) when it tripped, so a
 * `413 Payload Too Large` responder can report both.
 *
 * ## Hierarchy
 *
 * Like the other HTTP parse faults, this descends from the intermediate
 * [`HttpException`](HttpException.cajeta) → [`cajeta.net.NetException`](../NetException.cajeta)
 * root (NET-7.7), so it is catchable as `HttpException` (every HTTP
 * request-level fault) or the `NetException` root. The
 * `(message, limit, observed)` constructor mirrors
 * [`HeadersTooLargeException`](HeadersTooLargeException.cajeta)'s shape.
 *
 * ## The inherited `kind`
 *
 * As a `NetException`, every instance carries the cross-platform
 * [`kind`](../NetException.cajeta) ordinal, classified to
 * [`NetException.KIND_INVALID`](../NetException.cajeta) (12) — the whole
 * HTTP family's bucket — since an over-cap body is an invalid-input abuse,
 * not an errno-derived socket error. The crossed ceiling and the size
 * reached ride on `limit` / `observed`.
 */
public class PayloadTooLargeException extends HttpException {
    /** The configured body-size ceiling (bytes) that was crossed. */
    public int64 limit;
    /** The body size (bytes) reached when the cap tripped. */
    public int64 observed;

    public PayloadTooLargeException(String message, int64 limit, int64 observed) {
        this.message = message;
        this.cause = 0;
        this.kind = 12;   // NetException.KIND_INVALID (via HttpException)
        this.limit = limit;
        this.observed = observed;
    }

    /**
     * `413 Payload Too Large` — the status an HTTP server answers when an
     * inbound request body crosses the configured size cap. Overrides
     * [`HttpException.httpStatus`](HttpException.cajeta)'s `400` default so
     * the [`HttpServer`](HttpServer.cajeta) request loop maps an over-cap
     * body to `413` by virtual dispatch (the same RTTI-free mapping
     * [`HeadersTooLargeException`](HeadersTooLargeException.cajeta) uses for
     * `431`).
     */
    public int32 httpStatus() {
        return 413;
    }
}
